# openapi-typescript@7 declares a peer dependency on typescript@^5.x, and this project
# runs typescript@6. The generator works correctly against 6 — every type in
# src/api/schema.d.ts is produced by it — so the constraint is stale rather than real.
#
# Without this line npm refuses to install anything at all, including on a fresh clone,
# which turns a stale peer range into a broken checkout. Revisit when openapi-typescript
# widens the range; the fix then is deleting this file, not editing it.
legacy-peer-deps=true
